M(2,'Marketable surplus is:', ['Total farm output','Output remaining for sale after the farmer’s own requirements','Only imported food','Government tax revenue'],1,'It is the portion available for the market.')
M(2,'The Karve Committee (1955) is associated with:', ['Small-scale industries','Demonetisation','WTO establishment','Currency devaluation'],0,'It recognised small industries’ contribution to rural development and employment.')
M(2,'Equity as a planning goal emphasises:', ['Benefits reaching all sections and meeting basic needs','Only a rise in total output','Only imported machinery','Eliminating all private firms'],0,'Growth and equity are distinct: higher GDP alone does not ensure fair distribution.')
M(2,'Assertion: Initial Green Revolution gains were regionally uneven. Reason: Access to irrigation and complementary inputs varied across regions.', ['Both true; reason explains assertion','Both true; reason does not explain assertion','Assertion true; reason false','Assertion false; reason true'],0,'Regions with irrigation and resources could adopt the package more effectively.','Assertion–reason')
M(2,'Which is an argument AGAINST indiscriminate input subsidies?', ['They can encourage excessive water and chemical use','They always raise government revenue','They eliminate all inequality','They make every crop organic'],0,'Fiscal burdens and ecological damage are central criticisms, alongside unequal benefits.')
M(2,'A mixed economy has:', ['Only private ownership','Only government ownership','Both public and private sectors','No planning or markets'],2,'India combined public-sector leadership with regulated private enterprise.')
M(2,'Modernisation includes:', ['Only machinery, with no change in social outlook','Technology and progressive changes in social outlook','Only land ceilings','Complete withdrawal from foreign trade'],1,'The textbook includes social attitudes, such as women’s participation, alongside technology.')
