M(3,'LPG stands for:', ['Licensing, planning, grants','Liberalisation, privatisation, globalisation','Labour, prices, growth','Loans, production, government'],1,'These are the three main elements of the New Economic Policy.')
M(3,'Selling a minority government shareholding without transferring control is:', ['Necessarily full privatisation','Disinvestment','Nationalisation','Import substitution'],1,'Disinvestment can occur without a transfer of management control.')
M(3,'Statement I: Liberalisation reduces certain direct controls. Statement II: It eliminates all government regulation.', ['Both true','Both false','I true; II false','I false; II true'],2,'Prudential, safety and competition regulation can remain.','Two statements')
M(3,'An official reduction in currency value in a fixed or managed arrangement is:', ['Appreciation','Devaluation','Revaluation','Informalisation'],1,'Distinguish devaluation from market-driven depreciation.')
