M(4,'Assertion: Migration can be an investment in human capital. Reason: Its costs may be undertaken to obtain higher future earnings.', ['Both true; reason explains assertion','Both true; reason does not explain assertion','Assertion true; reason false','Assertion false; reason true'],0,'Travel and settlement costs are weighed against expected returns.','Assertion–reason')
M(4,'Which distinction is correct?', ['Human capital is separable from its owner','Physical capital is intangible','Human capital is inseparable from its owner','Human capital cannot ever lose value'],2,'A person supplies the services of human capital; the capability is embodied in that person.')
